SUMMARY:Silent Lake Loop
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **This adventure is sold out. Please [join the waitlist on our website.](h
 ttps://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/silent-lake-loop)**\n**This adve
 nture is exclusive to Explorer members.**\n**We’ve wanted to hike this t
 rail for years. There’s 15km of undeveloped shoreline with very few peop
 le around a beautiful looped trail. We finally have the opportunity to tac
 kle it in this Explorer exclusive.**\nThe Shoreline Trail starts from the 
 day use lot on a flat\, easy path that eases the group in. From there it s
 ettles beside the water and stays close to it for the rest of the hike\, w
 ith the lake appearing and disappearing through the trees.\nThe scenery sh
 ifts every few kilometres as the trail moves between low\, shaded ground a
 nd higher\, drier forest. Viewpoints along the way give us places to stop 
 and look out over the water\, and we’ll take a long lunch at one of them
 .\nIt’s a small group and a long trail\, which means plenty of time to t
 alk. By the time we reach lunch at the lookout\, the conversation will hav
 e covered about as much ground as the trail.\nCheck the trip plan (availab
 le on the website after registration) for the details\, including the meet
 ing point\, gear list\, and timing for the day.\n**Accessibility**\nWilder
 ness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible
 . If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or
  provide feedback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessuni
 on.com\n**Highlights**\n**Silent Lake Lookouts:** Most of the park’s loo
 kout points are along this trail\, with wide views across the water.\n**Is
 olated Landscape:** A day with a trail entirely to yourself.\n**Beaver Mea
 dows:** The trail crosses open meadow flats where beavers have reshaped th
 e landscape. It’s a good stretch for spotting birds and watching the lig
 ht change\n**Itinerary**\n**06:30** \\- Shuttle leaves from near Keele sta
 tion\n**10:00 - 16:00** \\- Hike Shoreline trail\n**16:00** \\- Anticipate
 d return to cars\n**19:30** \\- Anticipated return to Toronto\n**Event cos
 t: $65+HST. $60 optional transport also available. Join the waitlist [here
 .](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/silent-lake-loop)**\n**About
  Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outd
 oors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoor
 s and helps you find your people.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The
  group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada 
 and abroad.\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event a
 ttendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large
  enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not ov
 erwhelming!\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https:
 //www.wildernessunion.com/)***
