SUMMARY:Niagara Falls on Foot
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/niagara-falls)**\n**Most p
 eople who come to Niagara Falls stop at the railing. We’re going beyond 
 the falls\, to the part most visitors never see.**\nWe’ll start where ev
 eryone starts\, on the path beside the falls. It’s busy\, so we’ll tak
 e our time\, find a good spot\, and get the photos done before the crowds 
 thicken.\nThen we leave the crowds behind. A short drive away is the Niaga
 ra Glen Nature Reserve\, a protected pocket of forest deep inside the gorg
 e. We’ll take the stairways down to the river and hike a 6km loop along 
 the Niagara River that ends at the Whirlpool. On the way we’ll wind thro
 ugh huge boulders scattered across the gorge floor\, stopping for lunch on
  one of the flat spots in the reserve and moving at a pace that works for 
 the group.\nSee the falls from above\, then walk the river below as the go
 rge walls rise on either side. Both ends of the same river\, in one day.\n
 Check the trip plan for the details\, including the meeting point\, gear l
 ist\, and timing for the day.\n**Because this adventure includes multiple 
 stops\, taking our shared transport is mandatory. Transport is included in
  the cost of this adventure.**\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is com
 mitted to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to 
 make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback
 \, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n**Highlig
 hts**\n**Niagara Falls:** The full weight of the Niagara River dropping ov
 er the edge\, with the roar and spray carrying along the gorge rim.\n**Bou
 lder Fields:** Large boulders left behind as the Niagara River eroded thro
 ugh the gorge\, now draped in mosses and ferns.\n**The Niagara Whirlpool:*
 * The river hits a bend in the gorge and has nowhere to go but around\, sp
 inning into a slow\, churning circle.\n**Itinerary**\n**08:00** \\- Shuttl
 e leaves from near Keele station\n**10:00 - 11:45** \\- Walk the Niagara F
 alls path\n**11:45 - 12:00** \\- Drive to Niagara Glen\n**12:00 - 15:30** 
 \\- Hike Niagara Glen and Whirlpool trails\\\, with a stop for lunch\n**15
 :30 - 18:00** \\- Drive back to Toronto\n**Event cost: $120+HST. Transport
 ation is included in the cost of the adventure. Please register [here.](ht
 tps://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/niagara-falls)**\n**About Wildern
 ess Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors com
 munity that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and he
 lps you find your people.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group i
 s a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abro
 ad.\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendanc
 e - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough 
 that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelmi
 ng!\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wi
 ldernessunion.com/)***
