SUMMARY:Muskoka Highlights Hike
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/muskoka-highlights)**\n**M
 uskoka’s best-known views and best-loved trails\, packed into one day ou
 t of the city.**\nWe meet in Toronto and ride out together\, so no one is 
 stuck behind a wheel after a day on the trails. First stop is Hardy Lake P
 rovincial Park\, where we walk the 7km loop at an easy pace. Expect a rugg
 ed shoreline path with tree roots and patches of bare rock\, and the lake 
 in view through the trees.\nAfter the lake\, we drive to Huckleberry Rock.
  The trail is short\, but it climbs steadily\, and the trees open up to a 
 wide slab of granite with Lake Muskoka spread out below. Locals have been 
 coming up here for over a century\, and it’s easy to see why. We’ll ta
 ke our time at the top.\nThe day finishes in Bracebridge. You’ll have ti
 me to walk the main street\, explore cute cafes and bookstores to find som
 ething hot to eat or drink\, and stretch your legs before the ride home. L
 astly\, we will check out Bracebridge falls before heading home.\nThe idea
  is simple: see what Muskoka does best\, from a lakeside trail to a big op
 en view to a small town worth wandering. We take care of the planning and 
 the driving\, so all you need to do is show up and enjoy it.\nCheck the tr
 ip plan for the details\, including the meeting point\, gear list\, and ti
 ming for the day.\n**Because this adventure includes multiple stops\, taki
 ng our shared transport is mandatory. Transport is included in the cost of
  this adventure.**\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to ma
 king our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an acco
 mmodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback\, please do
  so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n**Highlights**\n**Har
 dy Lake Boardwalk:** A wooden walkway over the water on the lake loop\, an
 d one of the most photographed spots in the park.\n**Huckleberry Rock Look
 out:** A short climb up to an open clearing with sweeping views across Lak
 e Muskoka and the forest beyond.\n**Explore Bracebridge:** A small town on
  the Muskoka River\, with local shops\, cafés\, and places to eat.\n**Iti
 nerary**\n**08:00** \\- Shuttle leaves from near Keele station\n**10:30 - 
 14:00** \\- Hike Hardy Lake trail with a stop for lunch along the way\n**1
 4:00 - 14:30** \\- Drive to Huckleberry Rock\n**14:30 - 15:00** \\- Hike t
 o Huckleberry Rock viewpoint\n**15:00 - 15:20** \\- Drive to Bracebridge\n
 **15:20 - 16:30** \\- Explore Bracebridge\n**19:00** \\- Anticipated retur
 n to Toronto\n**Event cost: $120+HST. Transportation is included in the co
 st of the adventure. Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.c
 om/adventures/muskoka-highlights)**\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWildernes
 s Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that connects y
 ou to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find your peop
 le.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals 
 and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\nAttendance number
 s on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 
 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there's someone n
 ew to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n***Learn more at 
 our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
