SUMMARY:Survivalist Series: Firecraft Level 1
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fire-craft-intro-5)**\n***
 Discover the ancient art of safely creating and maintaining fire without l
 ighters or matches!***\nFor thousands of years\, fire has been our greates
 t ally for warmth\, safety\, cooking\, and survival. But in the wild\, fir
 e doesn’t come easy. It takes knowledge\, patience\, and the right techn
 ique.\nWe are back for another installment of this popular course to teach
  you the beautiful art of fire. You’ll begin to master the craft with ha
 nds-on guidance from our expert firecraft instructor - guide Kyle.\nYou'll
  be shown and encouraged to practice:\n1\\. Ferrocerium rod techniques wit
 h multiple tinders\n2\\. Traditional flint & steel fire lighting\n3\\. How
  to reliably start an effective fire\nThis course will give you the founda
 tion to create fire anywhere\, anytime.\n**Included:** Your own high-quali
 ty ferro rod to take home and keep the fire burning wherever you go.\n**Ne
 ed a knife?** You'll be using a knife throughout the day\, so a fixed-blad
 e knife is essential. If you don't have one\, you can purchase a high qual
 ity Mora knife during your check out. Please note that a knife is required
  for this course!\n**Who It’s For:** This course is for beginners and in
 termediate survivalists alike. Bring your curiosity\, a willingness to lea
 rn\, and a love of getting outside. This is an amazing opportunity not onl
 y to learn from our expert\, but it's a fun\, practical lesson at a unique
 ly low price.\n**About this series:** The Survivalist Series is an expert-
 led set of courses designed to develop applicable and life-saving skills i
 n the outdoors. Keep your eyes peeled for more courses on many other topic
 s coming soon!\n**Due to the cost of parking at Bronte Creek\, WU transpor
 t is recommended for this course.**\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union i
 s committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wis
 h to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provide fee
 dback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n**Hi
 ghlights**\n**Ancient techniques:** Learn unique firecraft techniques from
  long ago that do not need matches or a lighter.\n**Survivalist skills tra
 ining:** Develop essential skills to survive and thrive in the wild.\n**Fi
 re kit included:** Every participant gets this kit including a ferro rod a
 nd variety of tinders.\n**Itinerary**\n**10:00** \\- Shuttle leaves from n
 ear Keele station\n**11:00** \\- Arrive at course location\n**11:00 - 16:0
 0** \\- Introduction to fire craft course\n**16:00 - 17:00** \\- Drive bac
 k to Toronto\n**Event cost: $95+HST. $50 optional transport also available
 . Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fire-
 craft-intro-5)**\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is delibera
 te about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-chan
 ging magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\nMembers range 
 from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to To
 ronto from within Canada and abroad.\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't r
 eflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community mem
 bers at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but smal
 l enough that it's not overwhelming!\n***Learn more at our website [www.wi
 ldernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
