SUMMARY:Winter Solstice Night Hike
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **This adventure is sold out. Please [join the waitlist on our website.](h
 ttps://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/solstice-night-hike)**\n**This a
 dventure is exclusive to Explorer members.**\n**The longest nights of the 
 year are a good time to experience a true adventure.**\nWe’ll start afte
 r dark at the main lot and head out on the Beaver Dam Trail\, then link in
 to sections of the Bruce Trail and the Hilton Falls Side Trail. It’s a f
 ull 21km\, half marathon distance\, so it suits people who are comfortable
  moving at a steady pace for hours in the cold.\nEveryone hikes by headlam
 p. Somewhere along the route we’ll find a quiet stretch\, switch them al
 l off\, and give our eyes a few minutes to adjust. If the sky cooperates\,
  there will be stars. If it doesn’t\, you still get the silence of a win
 ter forest at night.\nWe’ll also pass the falls and the old mill ruins o
 n the way through. Bring a thermos\, dress for standing still as well as m
 oving\, and expect to finish tired\, cold-cheeked and very awake.\nCheck t
 he trip plan for the details\, including the meeting point\, gear list\, a
 nd timing for the day.\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed t
 o making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an 
 accommodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback\, pleas
 e do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n**Highlights**\n*
 *Hiking After Dark:** Your view shrinks to the beam of your headlamp\, and
  you hear more than you see. It’s the same trail we hike by day\, covere
 d at night.\n**Half Marathon Distance:** 21km with 201 m of elevation gain
 \, in winter conditions and by headlamp.\n**Headlamps Off:** A planned sto
 p where the whole group switches off and waits for our eyes to adjust. Wea
 ther permitting\, it’s the best chance on the route to see stars.\n**Iti
 nerary**\n**21:00** \\- Shuttle leaves from near Keele station\n**22:00** 
 \\- Arrive at the trailhead\n**22:00 - 06:30** \\- Hike trail overnight\n*
 *06:30 - 07:30** \\- Drive back to Toronto\n**Event cost: $60+HST. $40 opt
 ional transport also available. Join the waitlist [here.](https://www.wild
 ernessunion.com/adventures/solstice-night-hike)**\n**About Wilderness Unio
 n**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community t
 hat connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you 
 find your people.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix 
 of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\nAtt
 endance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we t
 ypically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that the
 re's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n***
 Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wilderness
 union.com/)***
